* System-level harness for staged integration (LTspice export)
* Converted from 90_system_integration_harness.cir

* Partial integration: B0 + B1 + B2

.include 00_block_b0_pv_input_ltspice_inc.cir
.include 01_block_b1_power_stage_ltspice_inc.cir
.include 02_block_b2_battery_boundary_ltspice_inc.cir
* .include 03_block_b3_control_rail_ltspice.cir
* .include 04_block_b4_fault_network_ltspice.cir
* .include 05_block_b5_measurement_frontend_ltspice.cir

* Keep this harness focused on integration transients and corner sweeps.

.temp 25

.tran 50n 4m

* Key observability points from the original harness
* Node meanings for this staged harness:
* PV_IN_POS_RAW = raw PV receiver node before fuse/TVS
* PV_IN_POS_FUSED = protected PV node after fuse/TVS
* PV_IN_POS = simplified converter input rail
* V_out = simplified buck output node
* CHG_OUT_POS = charger-side boundary before the battery fuse
* BAT_BUS_POS = battery terminal / pack bus node
* SW_1 / SW_2 = internal switching nodes of the simplified power stage
.print tran V(PV_IN_POS_RAW) V(PV_IN_POS_FUSED) V(PV_IN_POS)
.print tran V(V_out) V(CHG_OUT_POS) V(BAT_BUS_POS)
.print tran V(SW_1) V(SW_2)
.print tran I(V_CHG_PROBE)

* End-of-run checks for quick automation
* Target-analysis note: for the current 12.8V LiFePO4-style battery assumption, the simplified model should stay in the 12A charging band if the power-stage and loss assumptions remain in bounds.
.meas tran VOUT_FINAL FIND V(V_out) AT=4m
.meas tran BAT_FINAL FIND V(BAT_BUS_POS) AT=4m
.meas tran ICHG_FINAL FIND I(V_CHG_PROBE) AT=4m

* Lightweight corner sweep notes for the next validation pass:
* 1) PV input variation: VIN from 30V to 36V
* 2) Battery load variation: pack leakage and ESR changes
* 3) Check that the simplified model remains in a plausible charging band rather than collapsing to an obvious failure mode
* Current baseline interpretation: the simplified model now yields a stable charging-like response around 14.6V output, 13.95V battery bus, and ~14A charge current, so it is suitable for concept-level sanity checking but not yet hardware proof.

.end